From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:19:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libxess: Answer XeSS on D3D12 with MetalFX through DXMT.

XeSS's network ran SMITE 2 at ~4 FPS on Apple GPUs (DP4a, emulated);
patch 0022 made libxess report every device unsupported. MetalFX's
temporal upscaler does the same job in ~2-3 ms at 1440p. Keep XeSS's
API and hand the frame to MetalFX through DXMT's private D3D12
interface (MacNeutron's DXMT patches 0004-0005).

d3d12.c implements the D3D12 calls a game makes:

- xessD3D12CreateContext queries the device for IMTLD3D12DeviceExt;
  without it (Wine's own D3D12) it stores NULL and returns
  XESS_RESULT_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_DEVICE (-1) as before.
- xessD3D12Init accepts init flags 0-8 and 30 (profiling) and refuses
  others (-4). It releases the context's upscaler and makes one for the
  usual textures (the mode's input, RGBA16F colour and output, D32
  depth, RG16F motion vectors); a failure fails Init (-5).
- xessD3D12Execute records one TemporalUpscale into the game's command
  list. It makes another upscaler when the textures' formats or flags
  differ from the upscaler's or when they don't hold the region it
  reads; within one, the content size can move (dynamic resolution).
  Jitter and motion vectors follow Intel's XeSS-SR Developer Guide 2.0:
  the jitter moves the samples by -jitter, and motion vectors point
  from the current frame to the previous one (MetalFX's convention):
  both pass as they are, times xessSetJitterScale/xessSetVelocityScale
  (NDC velocity: times half the content size, y flipped).
- xessGetOptimalInputResolution: XeSS 1.3+'s ratios (AA 1.0, UQ+ 1.3,
  UQ 1.5, Q 1.7, B 2.0, P 2.3, UP 3.0), rounded down to even within
  MetalFX's range; the range runs from that size to the output's.
- xessGetIntelXeFXVersion is 0.0.0 off Intel GPUs; xessGetProperties
  asks for no descriptors or heaps; BuildPipelines, IsOptimalDriver,
  GetPipelineBuildStatus, GetInitParams, the scale getters and setters
  and the logging callback (WARN-level messages) are answered.

Contexts live in one locked list: a stale or foreign handle returns
XESS_RESULT_ERROR_INVALID_CONTEXT (-8) and is never dereferenced. Each
context has its own lock. A bad call returns XeSS's code, records
nothing and logs once; the first Init and the first Execute log their
parameters once as WARN, which the launcher's logging mode shows.

xess.h copies the declarations used from Intel's public headers
(github.com/intel/xess, branch main, MIT since commit de0fb9c) with
Intel's notice; dxmt_d3d12_ext.h is a C copy of DXMT's interface.
libxess_dx11 keeps 0022's stand-ins (it builds main.c only).

Local to MacNeutron; not proposed upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
